// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Society pool: survey and fieldwork mechanics, observation, time use,
// eyewitness lab studies, distance and access, audiences and adverts, and
// the logistics of running a service.
//
// The only pool for sociology and criminology; the main pool for human
// geography, anthropology, media & communication and social work.
//
// Everything here is methodological or plainly mechanical: a longer
// questionnaire is finished by fewer people, a longer delay before a line-up
// makes identification less accurate, a park further away is visited less
// often. Nothing compares groups of people by who they are, and nothing
// touches crime rates, policy, politics or outcomes for service users.
// Criminology items are lab studies with volunteers watching staged videos.
// Studies are done on human participants. See pools/README.md for the rules.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

